# "If <condition>, <body> instead[. Otherwise, <otherwise>]": a replacement applying only while
# `condition` holds, as "draw a card. If you control three or more artifacts, draw two cards
# instead" [CR#614.1a,614.15]. Otherwise the `otherwise` replacement applies, or with none the
# event happens unmodified. A replacement that already has a condition keeps it inside, and a
# caller's replacement stays its caller's.
primitive doIf(
  condition: Condition,
  body: Replacement,
  otherwise: Option(Replacement) = none): Replacement = OnlyIf {
  # TODO(spelling): Print ". Otherwise, <otherwise>" when otherwise is supplied.
  spelling = "If <condition>, <body> instead"
}
